= War in Gaza

Hamas has attacked Israel on October 7, killing some 1,200 people, and Israel has launched a devastating war in Gaza. American politics is torn: Jewish and Arab-American communities, the young, and the progressive base, and a majority of Americans, want different things.

- @gaza_israel: Stand firmly with Israel
- @gaza_ceasefire: Push for a ceasefire and humanitarian aid
- @gaza_conditional: Condition military aid

@gaza_israel
on-arrival: moderate_strength += 2; intl_relation += 2; left_relation -= 10; farleft_strength += 3; young_dem -= 4*(1-dissent); minority_dem -= 2*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent += 8

Support for Israel remains our official line; protests spread on campuses and the movement against us grows.

@gaza_ceasefire
on-arrival: left_relation += 4; farleft_strength -= 0.5; young_dem += 1*(1-dissent); progressive_dissent += 0; moderate_dissent += 4; intl_relation -= 2

We press for a ceasefire. Allies and critics are both unhappy.

@gaza_conditional
on-arrival: left_relation += 7; farleft_strength -= 1.5; progressive_dissent -= 4; moderate_dissent += 6; intl_relation -= 4; young_dem += 2*(1-dissent)

We demand conditions on aid; the old guard is furious.
